 succeeded in 0ms:
Stream what the child itself wrote to its provider log.

This is the live-reading surface. 'spawn observe' prints the durable
run-event ledger as one delta when the call returns at terminal state or
--timeout; 'spawn transcript' prints transcript lines incrementally while
following, so a consumer attached to a running child sees tool activity as
the log grows.

Dispatch is by the run's runtime id (state.json agent_type): muse runs
decode through the muse exec --json decoder to compact 'transcript:' lines,
and every other runtime prints raw tail lines unchanged.

Cursors are command-scoped, not ledger cursors: for muse the cursor is the
record sequence (RUN-ID:SEQ), for raw it is a byte offset (RUN-ID:OFFSET).
A transcript cursor resumes only 'transcript'; it never replays ledger
events and a ledger cursor never replays the transcript.

Usage:
  task-board spawn transcript <RUN-ID> [flags]

Flags:
      --allow-blocking           Block until terminal even from a manager-hosted orchestrator session (the in-session notice already reports the terminal run state)
      --cursor string            Resume cursor: <SEQ> or <RUN-ID>:<SEQ> (record sequence for muse, byte offset for raw)
      --format string            Output format: compact or json (default "compact")
  -h, --help                     help for transcript
      --poll-interval duration   Poll interval while following (default 500ms)
      --timeout duration         Maximum follow time (0 means no timeout)

Global Flags:
      --board-dir string         Path to the board directory (overrides TASK_BOARD_DIR and config local.board_dir) (default ".task-board")
      --context-profile string   Agent context profile override: full or lite
      --insecure                 Skip TLS certificate verification (for self-signed certs)
      --json                     Output in JSON format
      --no-update-check          Disable automatic update check
      --remote string            Remote board server URL (overrides TASK_BOARD_REMOTE)
      --remote-board string      Remote board ID (overrides TASK_BOARD_ID)

